60 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338649 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338649 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338649 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338649 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186337897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338649 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d281a134-374b-5aef-8d0d-6fbd0b5e1009" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339000 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339000 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71835" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339000 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339000 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=8$, $|\\,q\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Find the vector projection of $p$ onto $q$ in terms of the vector $q.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339000 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47b269c9-2c28-5ab1-9f15-6a708a836ca9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339000 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =|\\,p\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $q:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{q}{|\\,q\\,|}=\\frac{q}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}q\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,p & ={\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p\\cdot u \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}q \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}q\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339002 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339002 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71839" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339002 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339002 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=4\\sqrt{2}$, $|\\,q\\,|=16$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={45}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p$ in terms of the vector $p.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339002 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "405bd8b0-536b-5f37-9b2a-88044b8dd73a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339002 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =|\\,q\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =16\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $p:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{p}{|\\,p\\,|}=\\frac{p}{4\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}p\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & ={\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q\\cdot u \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}p \\\\  & =2p\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428209 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428209 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1295->1277. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428209 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186051021 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186441535 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 1759218