86045417] [17592186480639 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $a=⟨1,2,-1⟩$ and $b=⟨1,x,2⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480639 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1d98c763-a05e-5de6-913c-903735959780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480639 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2x-1 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480688 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186480600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480688 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126505" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480688 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480688 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=3$, $|\\,q\\,|=6\\sqrt{2}$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p$ in terms of the vector $p.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480688 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6749b1c-5bbb-5e2e-a55f-6596daa98287" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480688 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =|\\,q\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $p:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{p}{|\\,p\\,|}=\\frac{p}{3}=\\frac{1}{3}p\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & ={\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q\\cdot u \\\\  & =-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}p \\\\  & =-2p\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480692 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186480550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480692 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101544" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480692 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480692 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $p=⟨3,2,-1⟩$ and $q=⟨6,-1,8⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480692 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c61c8891-41ce-5169-9fd8-85b0f9123364" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480692 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{p\\cdot p}p \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 6+2\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 8}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{14}⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{12}{7},\\frac{8}{7},-\\frac{4}{7}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
